# Test: show mtu with an IKE engine that holds no tunnel says no-tunnels
# Spec: spec-path-mtu-diagnostic -- AC-18, the registered half
# VALIDATES: a daemon whose IKE engine is linked but configures no peer answers
#            `inventory` registered and verdict `no-tunnels`, with no note that
#            the inventory is unregistered. The other half of AC-18, a build
#            without the IKE engine answering `not-registered`, cannot be built
#            by the functional runner (one `ze` links every component), so
#            TestShowMTUNoInventoryIsNotZeroTunnels pins it over the seam.
# PREVENTS: an empty inventory read as an absent one, or the reverse.
#
# The path is three network namespaces joined by veth pairs, built by the
# compiled fixture `plugin/clamped-path` (internal/test/fixture, netlink): the
# daemon runs in the sender namespace, the router forwards with its far link at
# 1400, and the far namespace answers. Building them needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# the raw ICMP socket needs CAP_NET_RAW, so the test runs in the QEMU guest as
# root (`./le test qemu all-tests`) and skips in the unprivileged merge gate. The
# fixture removes the namespaces when the daemon exits, whatever its exit code.

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw

tmpfs=mtu-none.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external show-mtu-test {
		run "le-test fixture plugin/show-mtu-no-tunnels"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le-test fixture plugin/clamped-path netns zemtunone$PORT run ze start mtu-none.conf:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: a registered inventory with no tunnel answers verdict no-tunnels
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
